                        "review": "Let me preface this by saying this game isn't worth more than about $0.50 USD. If you can get it for that, or in a bundle, there's a small bit of fun to be had here. This is a perfect example of why Steam needs a \"meh\" option instead of just thumbs up or down. It's a 5 on a scale of 0-10.  It's better than most of the trash by Astro Port. So why would I recommend it ONLY for a severely discounted price? Because the game is like, 30 minutes long or so. You're going to play it once, complete it and the only other time you'll load it up is to farm the trading cards. It's just an average, forgettable game. As such, I can't recommend it.",
